I'm not sure which.

12:58.397 --> 12:59.463
Probably the gray-haired one

12:59.498 --> 13:01.099
with the whiskey-face sunburn?

13:01.134 --> 13:02.800
Oh, it's an honor to meet you, sir.

13:02.836 --> 13:04.102
You must be very proud.

13:04.137 --> 13:05.103
Hell yeah.

13:05.138 --> 13:06.470
I think every dad's dream

13:06.505 --> 13:08.806
is taking his son's sloppy seconds.

13:08.842 --> 13:10.441
Is your mom here, too?

13:10.476 --> 13:11.575
They don't have a mom.

13:11.611 --> 13:12.910
My ex-wife raised them,

13:12.946 --> 13:14.645
God bless her, but genetically,

13:14.680 --> 13:17.948
they're a product of me
blammin' onto a side of beef.

13:20.986 --> 13:22.986
All right, since we sold out so fast,

13:23.021 --> 13:24.888
we've got to make these
bees more productive,

13:24.923 --> 13:26.123
get them to make more honey.

13:26.158 --> 13:27.290
How are we gonna do that?

13:27.325 --> 13:28.792
Steroids, Brian.

13:28.827 --> 13:30.260
This here is the same stuff

13:30.295 --> 13:31.827
that turned Barry Bonds' head

13:31.863 --> 13:33.729
into a prize-winning squash.

13:33.765 --> 13:35.731
Okay. Well, how much are
we supposed to give them?

13:35.767 --> 13:36.766
Hmm.

13:36.801 --> 13:39.101
It says this is enough for a horse, so,

13:39.137 --> 13:41.170
I don't know, how many bees is a horse?

13:41.205 --> 13:42.972
Well, you can't fit a horse in this box,

13:43.007 --> 13:44.974
so I'd just use the whole thing.

13:45.009 --> 13:46.142
That makes sense.

13:49.379 --> 13:52.647
Barry Bonds says that's
too much steroids.

13:52.682 --> 13:54.448
Time for bed, Barry.

14:04.795 --> 14:06.293
God, they're still going?

14:06.328 --> 14:08.528
Peter, this is exactly what
I told you would happen!

14:08.563 --> 14:10.630
Not so much fun anymore, is it?

14:10.666 --> 14:12.166
Oh, thank God,

14:12.201 --> 14:14.001
maybe they're wrapping it up.

14:20.575 --> 14:22.176
Damn it, I can't take anymore!

14:22.211 --> 14:24.177
He is the worst neighbor ever.

14:24.212 --> 14:26.145
You won't believe what he did yesterday.

14:27.215 --> 14:28.647
Hey, Grover, catch!

14:40.660 --> 14:42.493
Uh, listen, Gronk, um,

14:42.529 --> 14:44.029
it's gettin' kind of late.

14:44.064 --> 14:46.497
Don't you think maybe it's
time to call it a night?

14:46.533 --> 14:47.532
Yeah, sure.

14:47.567 --> 14:49.500
Hey, you ever seen a nard explode?

14:49.536 --> 14:51.469
A... a what? A wha... a nard?

14:51.504 --> 14:52.704
I don't...

14:52.739 --> 14:54.005
Is that something on the Internet?

14:54.041 --> 14:55.073
Uh, 'cause I...

14:55.108 --> 14:56.341
Ah, damn it, what the hell?!

14:57.376 --> 14:58.709
Oh, nice shot there.

14:58.744 --> 15:00.377
Come on, don't get mad, bro.

15:00.412 --> 15:01.478
I was just kidding.

15:01.513 --> 15:02.479
You were kidding?!

15:02.514 --> 15:03.547
What was the joke?!

15:03.582 --> 15:04.681
This was!

15:04.717 --> 15:06.550
Oh, damn it, you hit the seam!

15:06.585 --> 15:07.718
Oh!

15:07.753 --> 15:08.719
Yeah.

15:08.754 --> 15:09.720
You know what?

15:09.755 --> 15:11.322
You're a jerk, Gronk!

15:11.357 --> 15:12.323
That's it,

15:12.358 --> 15:13.724
I'm getting rid of that bastard.

15:13.759 --> 15:15.225
Just like I helped kick the British

15:15.260 --> 15:16.659
out of America.

15:16.694 --> 15:19.262
This tyranny shall not stand!

15:19.297 --> 15:20.830
For without liberty...

15:20.866 --> 15:22.832
Ah, crap, he's even in the cutaways!

15:24.903 --> 15:27.536
Just...
Just go to commercial.

15:27.572 --> 15:29.405
I'm gonna squat here
and hold onto this bench.

15:36.413 --> 15:38.313
Peter, you got to figure something out.

15:38.349 --> 15:40.315
They haven't stopped
partying the whole night.

15:40.351 --> 15:41.583
- Yeah!
- Gronk!

15:41.618 --> 15:43.551
- Party!
- I'm the dad!

15:43.587 --> 15:45.587
I'm sorry, you were right all along.

15:45.622 --> 15:46.922
But don't worry, I'll take care of it.

15:46.957 --> 15:48.656
Well, you better do something soon.

15:48.692 --> 15:49.992
I can't live like this.

15:50.027 --> 15:51.558
I know. That guy's more annoying

15:51.594 --> 15:52.994
than going to an Italian restaurant

15:53.029 --> 15:54.896
with someone who's been to Italy.

15:54.931 --> 15:56.597
They call this a trattoria?

15:56.632 --> 15:58.565
More like a ristorante to me.

15:58.601 --> 16:00.401
Look at that fresco.

16:00.436 --> 16:02.236
Supposed to be the hills of Elba?

16:02.272 --> 16:03.905
Not once you've seen 'em.

16:03.940 --> 16:04.906
Are you ready to order?

16:04.941 --> 16:07.074
Si. Let me handle this, Peter.

16:07.110 --> 16:10.143
Two spaghettis and a chicken fingers.

16:14.413 --> 16:16.449
God, look at all the
honey the bees made!

16:16.484 --> 16:18.718
Those steroids were
a great idea, Stewie.

16:18.753 --> 16:21.454
Hey, look, that bee is
trying to get our honey.

16:21.489 --> 16:22.956
Okay, Mr. Bee,

16:22.991 --> 16:24.757
we'll give you the employee discount.

16:24.793 --> 16:25.757
After all, you...

16:25.793 --> 16:27.259
Holy crap!

16:27.295 --> 16:29.561
That thing just lifted
a whole jar of honey!

16:29.596 --> 16:33.265
Oh, God, do you think that's
one of our steroid bees?

16:35.136 --> 16:37.202
Well, this one's wearing
a hoodie as a shirt.

16:37.238 --> 16:39.471
So, yeah, I think these are ours.

16:39.506 --> 16:40.973
Stewie, I have a bad feeling abo...

16:41.008 --> 16:42.907
Oh, God, it just ate the other bee!

16:42.943 --> 16:45.944
Okay, so a few of them
had a bad reaction to...

16:45.979 --> 16:47.278
Oh, crap.

16:51.151 --> 16:53.351
Oh, my God. Brian, run!

16:58.258 --> 17:00.424
I think maybe giving those bees steroids

17:00.459 --> 17:01.658
was a bad idea.

17:02.694 --> 17:04.661
Turn on the wipers!

17:12.871 --> 17:14.137
You sure this is gonna work, Peter?

17:14.173 --> 17:15.272
Absolutely.

17:15.307 --> 17:17.340
Gronk went to the University of Arizona,

17:17.375 --> 17:19.741
and everyone who went to
the University of Arizona

17:19.777 --> 17:21.410
believes leprechauns are real.

17:21.446 --> 17:24.347
And since Cleveland already owns
a green suit and a top hat...

17:24.382 --> 17:26.715
This is my Easter clothes.

17:29.020 --> 17:30.652
Whoa, a leprechaun!

17:30.688 --> 17:31.854
Say the thing.

17:31.889 --> 17:32.921
Top
of the morning to you,

17:32.957 --> 17:34.155
Mr. Gronkowski.

17:34.191 --> 17:36.491
Have you any interest in a pot of gold?

17:36.526 --> 17:39.527
All you have to do is
move to Tallahassee!

17:39.562 --> 17:40.528
Wait a minute,

17:40.563 --> 17:42.430
this is just a disguise!

17:42.466 --> 17:44.699
Aah, son of a bitch!

17:44.734 --> 17:45.833
What's going on here?

17:45.869 --> 17:47.369
Are you guys trying to get rid of me?

17:47.404 --> 17:48.536
Yeah, we're tryin' to get rid of you!

17:48.571 --> 17:49.837
Why?

17:49.873 --> 17:52.172
'Cause you're a pain in
the ass to live next to!

17:52.208 --> 17:53.474
I mean, what the hell, Gronk?

17:53.509 --> 17:54.674
Why you got to be like this?

17:54.710 --> 17:55.809
You're a millionaire,

17:55.844 --> 17:57.444
you have the sweetest job in the world,

17:57.480 --> 17:58.812
you can do whatever you want.

17:58.847 --> 18:00.881
Why you got to act like
such an idiot all the time?

18:00.916 --> 18:03.283
It's not a choice, Grover.

18:03.319 --> 18:05.386
But rather, an obligation.

18:05.421 --> 18:07.053
You see, I've been groomed for this

18:07.088 --> 18:08.054
my entire life.

18:08.089 --> 18:09.622
Scoring touchdowns,

18:09.657 --> 18:10.623
making people laugh,

18:10.658 --> 18:11.991
punishing my body,

18:12.027 --> 18:13.326
enduring the pain.

18:13.361 --> 18:15.361
All in the name of entertainment.

18:15.397 --> 18:16.529
Don't you understand?

18:16.564 --> 18:18.364
I'm a commodity, a product.

18:18.400 --> 18:20.033
A modern day gladiator.

18:20.068 --> 18:22.068
You ask about the
whys and the wherefores

18:22.103 --> 18:23.403
behind the boorish facade?

18:23.438 --> 18:24.802
The answer is simple:

18:24.838 --> 18:28.240
I play the jester because
society deems it necessary.

18:29.276 --> 18:31.309
Also, I'm insane!

18:32.913 --> 18:33.878
Eat a butt, fatty!

18:33.914 --> 18:35.713
Gronk ain't going nowhere!

18:35.749 --> 18:37.249
Oh, that's it!

18:39.119 --> 18:40.885
Oh, cool, we're fighting?

18:40.921 --> 18:44.721
You guys mind if I eat
while I beat you up?

18:53.632 --> 18:55.199
What the hell are we supposed to do?

18:55.234 --> 18:56.233
We're surrounded!

18:56.269 --> 18:57.601
Hang on, I got this.

18:57.636 --> 18:59.669
"Meg, come outside.

18:59.704 --> 19:01.771
We have Pinkberry."

19:04.409 --> 19:06.209
Ow! Ow, ow! Stop... stop it!

19:06.244 --> 19:07.210
All right, they're distracted,

19:07.245 --> 19:08.911
let's go!

19:08.947 --> 19:10.780
Quick! We just have to
get rid of the queen!

19:10.815 --> 19:11.781
She's in the hive!

19:11.816 --> 19:12.949
What's that gonna do?

19:12.984 --> 19:14.750
The bees instinctively
stay with the queen,

19:14.786 --> 19:16.585
so if she's gone, they'll follow her!

19:16.620 --> 19:18.220
Okay, great, but how we gonna do it?

19:28.632 --> 19:30.265
You guys are bad fighters.

19:30.301 --> 19:31.800
That's his third sub.

19:34.137 --> 19:35.436
Ah, cool!

19:35.472 --> 19:36.937
Honey rain!

19:36.973 --> 19:37.938
Aah, oh, my God,

19:37.974 --> 19:38.939
is that a bee?!

19:38.975 --> 19:40.274
You have bees here?

19:40.310 --> 19:42.876
Uh, yeah, it's the world.

19:45.482 --> 19:46.481
Holy crap!

19:46.516 --> 19:47.482
There's a ton of them!

19:47.517 --> 19:49.216
Dad, start up the party bus!

19:49.251 --> 19:50.217
We're moving!

19:50.252 --> 19:51.218
Bees?

19:51.253 --> 19:52.219
Yeah, bees!

19:52.254 --> 19:53.286
And they're showing blitz!

19:53.322 --> 19:54.821
We got to leave on two!

20:00.929 --> 20:04.264
You think their Wi-Fi is "Vag-Town"?

20:04.299 --> 20:06.432
Yeah, that's probably them.

20:06.467 --> 20:08.867
Look at that, no password.

20:12.673 --> 20:14.106
Oh, well, thank goodness

20:14.142 --> 20:16.074
we finally have our neighborhood back.

20:16.110 --> 20:17.075
Yeah, now maybe Wilson

20:17.111 --> 20:18.110
can move back in and

20:18.146 --> 20:20.146
give me homespun wisdom over the fence.

20:20.181 --> 20:22.148
Peter, that was Home Improvement.

20:22.183 --> 20:23.681
It's exhausting

20:23.716 --> 20:26.083
that you never just go
with something I say.

20:26.119 --> 20:27.785
Coming up, yesterday's brisket.

20:29.556 --> 20:30.988
But first, breaking news:

20:31.024 --> 20:33.991
Rob Gronkowski has been
suspended from the Patriots

20:34.027 --> 20:35.660
following a failed drug test

20:35.695 --> 20:38.029
that showed evidence of
steroids in his system.

20:38.064 --> 20:40.264
The star athlete claims he has no idea

20:40.299 --> 20:42.432
how the banned substance
got into his body.

20:42.468 --> 20:43.500
Oh, no way!

20:43.536 --> 20:44.668
That's terrible.

20:44.703 --> 20:46.203
When pressed for further comment,

20:46.246 --> 20:48.012
Mr. Gronkowski said simply,

20:48.040 --> 20:49.606
"Grover, go long."

20:49.636 --> 20:50.689
Uh-oh.

20:51.667 --> 20:53.949
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru